\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ## Data Flow Explanation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
The 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 nl_query_service.py
\f1\fs24 \strokec2  script acts as the central brain of your backend. Using the data flow chart as our guide, here is how the service orchestrates the entire process after a user submits a query from the\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 React UI
\f1\b0 \strokec2 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 API Endpoint
\f1\b0 : The request is first received by the 
\f2\fs26 /api/query
\f1\fs24  endpoint defined in your 
\f2\fs26 main.py
\f1\fs24  file. This endpoint's only job is to pass the user's query to the 
\f2\fs26 process_nl_query
\f1\fs24  function within the service.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Intelligent Router
\f1\b0 : The first step inside the service is the 
\f0\b Intelligent Router
\f1\b0 . This component analyzes the user's question to determine its complexity.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Path 1: Simple Query
\f1\b0 : If the router decides the question is simple and direct (e.g., "List 5 ships"), it sends the query to the 
\f0\b Direct SQL Chain
\f1\b0 . This chain's role is to use an LLM (like the \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Gemini API
\f1\b0  ) to convert the question directly into a single, efficient SQL query, which is then executed against the \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b PostgreSQL DB
\f1\b0 .\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Path 2: Complex Query
\f1\b0 : If the router decides the question is complex or ambiguous (e.g., "Which type of ship was most common in the 19th century?"), it sends the query to the 
\f0\b SQL Agent
\f1\b0 . The agent is a more powerful tool that can reason, explore the database schema, and use multiple tools before generating and executing its final SQL query.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narrative Synthesizer
\f1\b0 : This is the final step orchestrated by the service. After either Path 1 or Path 2 has returned structured data from the \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b PostgreSQL DB
\f1\b0 , the service performs two actions:\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It uses the original query to search the \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Vector DB
\f1\b0  for relevant unstructured text (the RAG step).\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It sends both the structured data (from SQL) and the unstructured context (from the vector search) to the \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Narrative Synthesizer
\f1\b0 . This component uses a fast LLM (like \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Groq Llama 3
\f1\b0  ) to weave both sources of information into a single, human-readable narrative.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The service then packages this final narrative and the generated SQL into a JSON response to be displayed by the\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 React UI
\f1\b0 \strokec2 .\
}